 "what": "Synthetic end-of-day closes for the scoring tests. NOT market data.",
 "why": "The scoring tests used to derive their fixtures from whatever `prices_eod` happened to hold, which made them depend on an Alpaca key, on how much history had been ingested, and on today's date. On a fresh clone `make quickstart` loads one month, a 30-day horizon published 200 days ago has no entry session in it, and eight tests failed for a reason that had nothing to do with the code under test. Dates here are ABSOLUTE and in the past on purpose: a fixture anchored to `today` is a fixture that starts failing on a date nobody chose.",
 "licence": "These numbers are generated by the closed form recorded below. No vendor supplied them, so the redistribution terms that keep real closes off every screen in this product do not reach this file.",
